# Mutations for mutate.py. Each one swaps a piece of LocoWorkers.tla for a
# plausible bug and names the one property that must fail on it. The text
# after `- ` must occur exactly once in the spec; `+ ` lines replace it. An
# optional `only <label-substring>` line limits the matrix runs. Every property
# the matrix checks needs a mutation.

mutation a dequeued job is given an unknown owner
detects TypeOK
only workers=2 items=3 caller
- ELSE [owner EXCEPT ![j] = WorkerOwner(w)]
+ ELSE [owner EXCEPT ![j] = "orphan"]

mutation a worker takes a job without removing it from the queue
detects Ownership
only workers=2 items=3 caller
- /\ jobs' = Tail(jobs)
+ /\ jobs' = jobs

mutation pending Futures are resolved as a stack
detects DeliveryOrder
only workers=2 items=3 caller
- /\ current' = Head(pending) /\ pending' = Tail(pending)
+ /\ current' = pending[Len(pending)] /\ pending' = SubSeq(pending, 1, Len(pending) - 1)

mutation a failed Future is yielded as a result
detects NoDeliveryAfterFailure
only workers=2 items=3 caller
- Yields == outcome[current] = "ok"
+ Yields == outcome[current] \in {"ok", "err"}

mutation a failed Future is yielded before its error is raised
detects ErrorOrder
only workers=2 items=3 caller
- Yields == outcome[current] = "ok"
+ Yields == outcome[current] \in {"ok", "err"}

mutation one job more than the worker count is outstanding
detects WindowBound
only workers=2 items=3 caller
- /\ cpc' = IF Len(pending') = Workers THEN "pop" ELSE "pull"
+ /\ cpc' = IF Len(pending') = Workers + 1 THEN "pop" ELSE "pull"

mutation close keeps a settled Future
detects ClosedClean
only workers=2 items=3 caller
- /\ owner' = [i \in I |-> IF owner[i] \in {"future", "queue"} THEN "free" ELSE owner[i]]
+ /\ owner' = owner

# solve_eigen_pairs before its fix: workers started before the BLAS scope was
# entered, and a failure in either setup phase escaped cleanup.
mutation a failed worker start leaves the started workers running
detects SetupClean
only partial-start-failure
- Setup == [first |-> "scope", afterScope |-> "starting", afterStart |-> "pull", onError |-> "closing"]
+ Setup == [first |-> "starting", afterScope |-> "pull", afterStart |-> "scope", onError |-> "escaped"]

mutation a failed scope entry leaves every worker running
detects SetupClean
only scope-entry-failure
- Setup == [first |-> "scope", afterScope |-> "starting", afterStart |-> "pull", onError |-> "closing"]
+ Setup == [first |-> "starting", afterScope |-> "pull", afterStart |-> "scope", onError |-> "escaped"]

mutation cleanup restores the BLAS limits before joining the workers
detects ScopeCoversSolve
only workers=2 items=3 caller
- /\ scope' = IF cpc = "abandoning" THEN FALSE ELSE scope
+ /\ scope' = FALSE

mutation settling a Future does not wake the waiting consumer
detects CallsReturn
only workers=2 items=3 caller
- /\ cpc' = IF cpc = "wait" /\ current = held[w] THEN "await" ELSE cpc
+ /\ cpc' = cpc

mutation an enqueue does not wake the waiting workers
detects CallsReturn
only workers=1 items=1 drain
- Wake(ws) == [w \in W |-> IF ws[w] = "wait" THEN "ready" ELSE ws[w]]
+ Wake(ws) == ws

mutation shutdown sends no sentinels, so close never returns
detects CloseReturns
only workers=2 items=3 caller
- /\ jobs' = jobs \o [k \in 1..Workers |-> 0]
+ /\ jobs' = jobs

mutation shutdown sends no sentinels, so a full drain never finishes
detects DrainEnds
only workers=2 items=1 drain
- /\ jobs' = jobs \o [k \in 1..Workers |-> 0]
+ /\ jobs' = jobs

mutation the end of input is reported while Futures are still pending
detects EndOrder
only workers=2 items=1 drain
- /\ ended' = (Len(pending) = 0)
+ /\ ended' = TRUE
